A stray `}` ending a C-style block saved as a server script (issue #355,
the #351 follow-up found by the VS Code extension's corpus harness). The
parser forms no statement that starts with a closing delimiter, so the
line does not parse, and it gets no `;`: terminated, it left the next
line to start a statement of its own and formatting added an error. The
C-style line after it does not parse either and is left as written. The
input's only error, unmatched_delimiter, is all the output has.
-- input.ssl --
}
if (bReady) sText = Build(sText);
-- format --
}
if (bReady) sText = Build(sText);
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:2 error unmatched_delimiter: Unmatched '}'
2:1-2:3 warning direct_procedure_call: 'if' is not a known built-in function or in-file procedure. If it is a custom procedure, dispatch it via DoProc/ExecFunction; if it is a legacy vendor built-in, this call is valid as written.
2:21-2:26 warning direct_procedure_call: 'Build' is not a known built-in function or in-file procedure. If it is a custom procedure, dispatch it via DoProc/ExecFunction; if it is a legacy vendor built-in, this call is valid as written.
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
